0:{"buildId":"7afh9cBoHBO9HIwX4Lcyt","data":[{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","$L2",null,{"toc":[{"depth":2,"url":"#a-worker-is-oom-killed","title":"A worker is OOM-killed"},{"depth":3,"url":"#confirm-it","title":"Confirm it"},{"depth":3,"url":"#stop-the-bleeding","title":"Stop the bleeding"},{"depth":3,"url":"#make-it-stop-happening","title":"Make it stop happening"},{"depth":2,"url":"#the-disk-fills-up","title":"The disk fills up"},{"depth":3,"url":"#confirm-it-1","title":"Confirm it"},{"depth":3,"url":"#the-signal-to-look-for-first","title":"The signal to look for first"},{"depth":3,"url":"#stop-the-bleeding-1","title":"Stop the bleeding"},{"depth":3,"url":"#size-the-volume-for-twice-max_bytes","title":["Size the volume for twice ",["$","code",null,{"children":"max_bytes"}]]},{"depth":3,"url":"#two-layout-footguns","title":"Two layout footguns"},{"depth":2,"url":"#redis-fails-over","title":"Redis fails over"},{"depth":3,"url":"#what-actually-happens","title":"What actually happens"},{"depth":3,"url":"#what-breaks-depends-on-your-backend","title":"What breaks depends on your backend"},{"depth":3,"url":"#stop-the-bleeding-2","title":"Stop the bleeding"},{"depth":3,"url":"#configuration-worth-checking-now","title":"Configuration worth checking now"},{"depth":2,"url":"#the-queue-backpressures-and-never-recovers","title":"The queue backpressures and never recovers"},{"depth":3,"url":"#the-mechanism","title":"The mechanism"},{"depth":3,"url":"#confirm-it-2","title":"Confirm it"},{"depth":3,"url":"#stop-the-bleeding-3","title":"Stop the bleeding"},{"depth":3,"url":"#related-limits-that-block-rather-than-reject","title":"Related limits that block rather than reject"},{"depth":2,"url":"#every-build-stalls-and-nothing-errors","title":["Every build stalls at ",["$","code",null,{"children":"[Sched]"}]," and nothing errors"]},{"depth":2,"url":"#scheduler-redis-keeps-completed-actions","title":"The scheduler's Redis keeps every completed action"},{"depth":2,"url":"#restarting-the-scheduler","title":"Restarting the scheduler"},{"depth":2,"url":"#whats-next","title":"What's next"}],"children":[["$","$L3",null,{"children":"Runbooks"}],["$","$L4",null,{"children":"What to do when a Forge deployment is on fire: Redis failover, a worker OOM-killed, the disk full, and the queue backpressured. Each entry is a symptom, the signal that confirms it, the immediate action, and the change that stops it recurring."}],["$","$L5",null,{"children":["\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Who this is for:"}]," you are on call and something is broken right now.\n",["$","strong",null,{"children":"What you'll have at the end:"}]," for each of the four incidents Forge\nactually produces, a confirming signal, a stop-the-bleeding action, and the\nconfiguration change that prevents a repeat. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"Time:"}]," read once now, so you do\nnot read it for the first time at 03:00."]}],"\n",["$","div",null,{"data-prerequisites":true,"className":"my-6 rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface-elevated px-5 py-3","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"my-0 font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-brand","children":"Before you start"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground [&>p]:my-0","children":["$","p",null,{"children":"A deployment other people depend on."}]}]]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["These are incident procedures. They deliberately do not explain how Forge\nworks (",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/explanations/architecture","children":"Architecture"}]," does that) and they do not\ntune anything. When you have stopped the bleeding and want to make the system\nfaster rather than merely alive, go to ",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/operate/tuning","children":"Tuning"}],"."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["If you are not yet sure ",["$","em",null,{"children":"which"}]," incident you are having, start at\n",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/operate/troubleshooting","chil